// Rope Drop question bank (2026-11-26, Director: "Rope Drop", true trivia, one
// right answer, multiple choice only).
//
// Each question:
//   id   stable id. Never reuse or renumber: the daily schedule is built from ids.
//   r    rating: "g" green circle (10), "b" blue square (20),
//        "k" black diamond (30), "d" double black (50)
//   cat  resorts | apres | off | history | athletes | gear | snow | lingo
//   q    the question
//   a    the one right answer
//   w    three wrong answers. They must be plainly wrong, not "technically
//        also true" (see the Snowriver and Deer Valley notes below).
//   fact one line shown at the reveal, teaching a bit beyond the answer
//   src  where the fact comes from. "common" means everyday ski slang with no
//        single source. "app" means the app's own resort research
//        (src/data.js, research/apres.json, research/off-mountain.json). A URL
//        means it was checked against that page on 2026-11-26.
//   rid  optional: the resort the answer is about, for the "See resort" link
//
// Rules for writing more:
//  · Stable facts only (geography, history, records, terrain). No ticket
//    prices, owners or pass lists, which change every season.
//  · Never offer Indianhead and Blackjack against each other: they are now the
//    two halves of Snowriver.
//  · "Doesn't allow snowboarding" questions can't offer Alta, Deer Valley or
//    Mad River Glen as wrong answers. All three are skier-only.
//  · Resort state/province questions and the stat comparisons are generated in
//    app-rope-drop.js from data.js, so they aren't written out here.

